                        "sense_id": "457b15f3-fc02-3d4d-b857-7bb555346fd0",
                        "entry_id": "507aafaf-2e29-3985-81b4-54779dcedfd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualité, nature de ce qui est mystérieux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "71d17e2c-42bd-49ec-80f7-11631b807ae4",
                                "sense_id": "457b15f3-fc02-3d4d-b857-7bb555346fd0",
                                "text": "D’indépendance il se régale,\n Et sa mystériosité\n Esquive la société\n De sa grande sœur la cigale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9358dec0-5a88-4abd-9bf5-597abcafafc1",
                                "sense_id": "457b15f3-fc02-3d4d-b857-7bb555346fd0",
                                "text": "Curiosité éternelle, la mystériosité des femmes est un trésor à jamais enfoui."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b32f418f-7594-4a30-a747-4b0066bdf5a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "507aafaf-2e29-3985-81b4-54779dcedfd9",
                        "source_sense_id": "457b15f3-fc02-3d4d-b857-7bb555346fd0",
                        "target_lang_word": "mysteriousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mysteriousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab702c34-8f14-33ff-ad09-e2c471e66493",
                                        "entry_id": "297c8668-04d9-3360-a205-f475519f6819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being mysterious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b210aae0-c685-4548-baae-b6c7f461ca06",
                                                "sense_id": "ab702c34-8f14-33ff-ad09-e2c471e66493",
                                                "text": "1651, Jeremy Taylor, Twenty-Seven Sermons for the Summer Half-Year, Sermon II, Part II in ΕΝΙΑΥΤΟΣ: A Course of Sermons for All the Sundays of the Year, London: Tyler & Royston, 1668, p. 14, https://books.google.ca/books?id=heNBAQAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nThis may seem strange; and indeed it is so: and it is one of the great mysteriousnesses of the Gospel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "151e5cfe-9819-4ccb-bbb4-f4a1e66b809a",
                                                "sense_id": "ab702c34-8f14-33ff-ad09-e2c471e66493",
                                                "text": "This sort of mysteriousness, which is always so becoming in a hero, threw a fresh grace in Catherine's imagination around his person and manners, and increased her anxiety to know more of him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d582129-6e38-43c1-83f4-91923891ccc5",
                                                "sense_id": "ab702c34-8f14-33ff-ad09-e2c471e66493",
                                                "text": "His children had urged him to travel: Mary Chivers had felt sure it would do him good to go abroad and \"see the galleries.\" The very mysteriousness of such a cure made her the more confident of its efficacy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e14656d9-0214-476a-a1de-2e54467c4e2d",
                                                "sense_id": "ab702c34-8f14-33ff-ad09-e2c471e66493",
                                                "text": "And all this is not changed by adding \"mysterious\" experiences to \"manifest\" ones, self-confident in the wisdom that recognizes a secret compartment in things, reserved for the initiated, and holds the key, O mysteriousness without mystery, O piling up of information! It, it, it!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
